gtk4, fyne and bubbletea draw `ui.tabs` as tabs, where each drew sngl:ui's row
of buttons over the panels. gtk4's is a `Tabs`, gtk4rt's GtkStackSwitcher over
a GtkStack, and each tab a `TabPage` the stack holds; fyne's is
fynelayout.NewTabs, an AppTabs, with a fynelayout.TabPage per tab; bubbletea's
is a row of focusable `Styled` labels in tui.TabLook's boxes over the panels'
box. Every panel is still mounted with the tabs and hidden while another is
selected.

The page is what a test presses: its `@change` writes `selected` and emits
the tabs' `change(k)`, which is what lower.NamePresses looks for, and is named
for that event so the press and the invoker each target writes for it agree.
gtk4rt and fynelayout fire it only when the user, not the program, changes the
page shown. A tab an `if` writes reaches the stack, or the AppTabs, through the
render slot's insert into the tabs, and leaves through its remove.

`cmd/sngl/testdata/tabs_look_runs.txt` runs it, and
`tabs_look_cgo.txtar` builds gtk4's in cgo mode.

deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `"GtkButton"` -- a tab is a page of the stack, which the switcher shows
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `widget.NewButton` -- a tab is an AppTabs item

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import "sngl:test"

component strip ui.node {
    var idx = 0
    var changed = -1
    var extra = false

    ui.tabs #tabs(:selected=idx, style={padding=8px}, @change(i) {
        changed = i
    }) {
        ui.tab(label="One") {
            ui.text(value="first panel")
        }
        ui.tab(label="Off", disabled=true) {
            ui.text(value="second panel")
        }
        if extra {
            ui.tab(label="More") {
                ui.text(value="more panel")
            }
        }
    }
}

func testPressingATabSelectsIt(t test.Test, c strip) {
    c.extra = true
    c.tabs.change(2)
    t.assert(c.idx == 2)
    t.assert(c.changed == 2)
}

ui.window(title="t") {
    strip
}

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}
